{"_id":"68a7360f8ec3d8323af13253","nodeId":"fYjoXB4rnkM5gg46sqVz5","roadmapSlug":"computer-science","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:54.940Z","description":"# DNS\n\nThe Domain Name System (DNS) is the phonebook of the Internet. Humans access information online through domain names, like [nytimes.com](http://nytimes.com) or [espn.com](http://espn.com). Web browsers interact through Internet Protocol (IP) addresses. DNS translates domain names to IP addresses so browsers can load Internet resources.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"What is DNS?","url":"https://www.cloudflare.com/en-gb/learning/dns/what-is-dns/","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3c00"},{"type":"article","title":"How DNS works (comic)","url":"https://howdns.works/","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3c01"},{"type":"video","title":"DNS and How does it Work?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Wj0od2ag5sk","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3c02"},{"type":"video","title":"DNS Records","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7lxgpKh_fRY","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3c03"},{"type":"video","title":"Complete DNS mini-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zEmUuNFBgN8&list=PLTk5ZYSbd9MhMmOiPhfRJNW7bhxHo4q-K","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3c04"},{"type":"feed","title":"Explore top posts about DNS","url":"https://app.daily.dev/tags/dns?ref=roadmapsh","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3c05"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:02:21.077Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/computer-science/content/fYjoXB4rnkM5gg46sqVz5.md"}